From ceafc0f8fef0ceac432f132b9aca2c09459a833b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:11:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): refuse a wire taper the machine cannot post at the
 command door

A Wire Contour with a non-zero taper_deg is now refused by its create,
paste and edit commands (GUI and MCP) when the mounted machine states no
edm.max_taper_deg, the taper is past it, or a U/V machine states no guide
planes. The words come from app::machine::wire_edm::taper_door. Before, the
parameter was accepted and the cut was refused later, at generate or post.
No machine limit is guessed.

Fixes #1800

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
